& [DictatedClarification]
  + while work is active the lookahead remains loaded as key hints
  + the useful object should generally be lightweight and may be only one or two stitches
  + each stitch is ever-present throughout the exact work scope assigned to it
  + one stitch may draw a particular semantic turn into the main subject and carry one transform

& [SelectedAtomicUnit]
  + LookaheadStitch is the candidate smallest persistent unit of SOP Compiled Lookahead
  + a LookaheadPacket is zero or more ordered stitches plus packet identity and lifecycle rather than one mandatory large context block
  + the common case should prefer one or two high-signal stitches over a wide restatement of the whole SOP

& [StitchMeaning]
  + SubjectAnchor identifies the main subject whose trajectory is being guided
  + SemanticTurn identifies the distinction relationship orientation or conceptual move that should be drawn into reasoning about the subject
  + Transform identifies the bounded operation the semantic turn is intended to support
  + Scope identifies the objective phase feature requirement artifact or inference-pass interval in which the stitch remains applicable
  + KeyHints are the minimum terms identities coordinates or invariants needed to keep the turn salient
  + SourceBinding identifies where the stitch meaning and authority boundary came from
  + CompletionCue identifies the receipt observation or result that fulfills the stitch
  + Invalidators identify drift contradiction supersession scope exit or evidence that releases or replaces it

& [EverPresentProjection]
  + ever-present means the Cantor inference host deliberately projects the active stitch into every model invocation covered by its scope
  + the projection may be compact and need not repeat the complete SOP plan history or evidence body
  + the host preserves stitch identity and scope across stop tool result resume and reentry boundaries
  + a stateless model call does not remember the stitch unless the host reintroduces it
  + within a single context the stitch remains addressable input but no claim is made that it owns fixed attention weight hidden state K/V cache or a literal persistent neuron signal

& [SemanticTransform]
  + a stitch is not merely a keyword list because it binds terms to one intended semantic turn on the main subject
  + the turn may select a distinction conserve an invariant expose a relationship change level of abstraction bring a required counterexample into view or route attention toward an evidence gate
  + the transform remains a plan hint unless independently imported from a governing requirement
  + the model may reject or revise a derived transform when current evidence contradicts it

& [Lifecycle]
  + proposed means the compiler derived a candidate stitch but it is not projected
  + active means exact scope and source bindings pass and the host projects it into each covered inference call
  + fulfilled means its completion cue is present and a retained receipt closes the transform
  + invalidated means source state evidence or scope no longer corresponds
  + released means the scope ended and the stitch is no longer projected
  + replacement creates a new stitch identity rather than silently mutating an active one

& [LightweightBoundary]
  + a stitch should carry references and compact semantic coordinates rather than copying whole source files proofs transcripts or plans
  + the compiler should choose the smallest hint set that measurably prevents rediscovery or trajectory loss
  + every additional stitch spends context and increases anchoring risk so absence remains preferable when no measured benefit is expected
  + several interdependent stitches may be compiled as one batch only when their scopes and completion conditions are jointly conserved

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + this snapshot authorizes source custody and later SJS processing only
  + no canonical stitch schema satisfaction signature host projection prompt mutation provider call model modification performance claim autonomous work workspace mutation remote action FPGA Minecraft or physical effect is authorized
